Subject: [PATCH] calc: fix stale and truncated answers, copying, and history

- qalc's output is read to the end (it was cut at 4096 bytes and a larger
  one could fill the pipe and wedge qalc), and an answer that comes back
  for an input that has since changed is dropped instead of shown.
- Enter copies the answer and closes; if qalc has not caught up with the
  last keystroke, the current input is calculated first. With text typed,
  the top row always belongs to it ("No result" on an error) so Enter can
  never fall through to an old history entry.
- A warning no longer counts as an error: solving for x always warns that
  x is assumed real, which made equations impossible to copy.
- The copied value drops "approx.", uses ASCII operators and is passed to
  -calc-command shell-quoted; it was escaped with g_strescape, which turned
  every non-ASCII character (€, ², µ) into octal.
- History keeps what was typed alongside the answer, is rewritten whole on
  each change, skips duplicates, and Shift+Return brings an entry back into
  the input (or carries the current answer on). Old lines still load.
- kb-custom-1 copies the input text; rofi has no selection, and its own
  copy key is unimplemented on Wayland.
- Empty input clears the answer (rofi stops calling _preprocess_input once
  the entry is empty, and qalc with no expression printed its first-run
  autocalc question), -m stops runaway calculations, unicode signs are
  forced on, and a very long answer is clipped on screen (not when copied).
- Dropped: -reuse-result and -calc-command-history, now the default flow.
